00:08:57.740 --> 00:08:59.590
and then there's multiple different ways

00:08:59.590 --> 00:09:00.423
to read a Kanji.

00:09:00.423 --> 00:09:01.977
And then when you know both,
it's like, "Yeah, I'm kinda-

00:09:01.977 --> 00:09:03.980
- You're like that one Isekai protai

00:09:03.980 --> 00:09:06.480
who just comes in is
like, "What does this say?

00:09:06.480 --> 00:09:07.441
I don't know."

00:09:07.441 --> 00:09:08.727
And they're 12 episodes it, his like,

00:09:08.727 --> 00:09:09.858
"Yeah, I get it."

00:09:09.858 --> 00:09:10.720
(all laugh)

00:09:10.720 --> 00:09:12.447
- Yeah, it's been really
helpful for just learning.

00:09:12.447 --> 00:09:13.661
Speaking in general.

00:09:13.661 --> 00:09:17.560
Because a lot of the words
have the same pronunciation,

00:09:17.560 --> 00:09:19.740
and then obviously Kanji is
the way to differentiate it.

00:09:19.740 --> 00:09:21.680
- Yeah, Kanji holds the meaning, right?

00:09:21.680 --> 00:09:22.513
- Yeah.

00:09:22.513 --> 00:09:24.340
- And sometimes reading a
whole sentence in Hiragana

00:09:24.340 --> 00:09:25.350
is like a fucking nightmare.

00:09:25.350 --> 00:09:26.183
- It is a nightmare.

00:09:26.183 --> 00:09:29.920
And weirdly enough for
people who'd have no idea

00:09:29.920 --> 00:09:31.900
about Japanese it might
be hot to think about,

00:09:31.900 --> 00:09:35.670
but a full on Hiragana
or Katakana sentence

00:09:35.670 --> 00:09:37.830
is so difficult to read sometimes.

00:09:37.830 --> 00:09:38.767
Whereas Kanji is just like,

00:09:38.767 --> 00:09:40.910
"Oh yeah, I know exactly what that means.

00:09:40.910 --> 00:09:42.410
I know exactly how to read it."

00:09:42.410 --> 00:09:44.090
- The way I see it, is that in English,

00:09:44.090 --> 00:09:46.510
is that how we don't
need to read the word,

00:09:46.510 --> 00:09:47.774
we know the shape of the word.

00:09:47.774 --> 00:09:48.607
you know what I mean?

00:09:48.607 --> 00:09:49.440
- Yeah.

00:09:49.440 --> 00:09:50.273
- We can see a word.

00:09:50.273 --> 00:09:51.380
I know the shape of the
word, I can read it.

00:09:51.380 --> 00:09:53.780
And I think that's how
Kanji is to Japanese people.

00:09:53.780 --> 00:09:55.660
Where they don't necessarily read it

00:09:55.660 --> 00:09:57.940
but they recognize that the shape.

00:09:57.940 --> 00:09:59.803
And then they just know what's
being said in the sentence

00:09:59.803 --> 00:10:00.636
- Because have you seen that video

00:10:00.636 --> 00:10:03.660
where you can read an entire paragraph?

00:10:03.660 --> 00:10:06.950
Where if the word the
first letter is the same

00:10:06.950 --> 00:10:08.440
the last letter is the
same and then you swap

00:10:08.440 --> 00:10:09.273
all the letters in the middle,

00:10:09.273 --> 00:10:10.704
you can still read what's going on.

00:10:10.704 --> 00:10:13.910
Just because of how your fluency works.

00:10:13.910 --> 00:10:14.743
- Yeah.

00:10:14.743 --> 00:10:17.040
- I feel it would be the
same with Kanji as well.

00:10:17.040 --> 00:10:18.210
- I think so, yeah.

00:10:18.210 --> 00:10:19.043
It is the same.

00:10:19.043 --> 00:10:20.810
But instead of the first and last letters

00:10:20.810 --> 00:10:23.540
it's like does this have
one line in it or two?

00:10:23.540 --> 00:10:26.010
It's that but just squinting really hard.

00:10:26.010 --> 00:10:29.090
- Yeah, there are some
where there's so many lines

00:10:29.090 --> 00:10:30.950
where I'm like, "How the fuck do people

00:10:30.950 --> 00:10:32.070
just read it this fast?"

00:10:32.070 --> 00:10:34.360
- I mean the more difficult
is when you start to write it.

00:10:34.360 --> 00:10:35.244
Right?

00:10:35.244 --> 00:10:36.077
- Yeah, true, true.

00:10:36.077 --> 00:10:36.910
- That's when it starts to get difficult.

00:10:36.910 --> 00:10:37.964
- Yeah, because I have an app

00:10:37.964 --> 00:10:40.130
and it vibrates my phone if
you do the wrong stroke order.

00:10:40.130 --> 00:10:41.629
(all laugh)

00:10:41.629 --> 00:10:42.519
(Connor grunting)

00:10:42.519 --> 00:10:44.090
- No.

00:10:44.090 --> 00:10:45.900
- It's like, "That's not how you do it."

00:10:45.900 --> 00:10:46.780
It's been good though,

00:10:46.780 --> 00:10:49.330
because whenever write
a Kanji out in my class

00:10:49.330 --> 00:10:50.360
in the right stroke order.

00:10:50.360 --> 00:10:51.707
The teacher is like

00:10:51.707 --> 00:10:52.540
(Connor grunting)

00:10:52.540 --> 00:10:53.792
Like in the TV shows.

00:10:53.792 --> 00:10:54.625
- Like, "Why?"

00:10:54.625 --> 00:10:55.683
- What the fuck?

00:10:56.770 --> 00:10:58.190
Because you never really think about

00:10:58.190 --> 00:10:59.530
something like strike order.

00:10:59.530 --> 00:11:00.363
You know what I mean?

00:11:00.363 --> 00:11:03.570
Which stroke order is basically
the order you write it in.

00:11:03.570 --> 00:11:05.710
- Yeah, because I write my
Ss the wrong way in English

00:11:05.710 --> 00:11:06.543
and people freaking out.

00:11:06.543 --> 00:11:07.849
- I've seen you write your S.

00:11:07.849 --> 00:11:10.003
- Tell people how you write your Ss?

00:11:11.617 --> 00:11:12.930
- You're supposed to do
it top to bottom right?

00:11:12.930 --> 00:11:14.786
- Yeah, most people do it like that.

00:11:14.786 --> 00:11:15.619
- Like that.

00:11:15.619 --> 00:11:16.457
- I do it from top to bottom up.

00:11:16.457 --> 00:11:18.320
And then swish down with the cursive.

00:11:18.320 --> 00:11:20.160
I don't know why.

00:11:20.160 --> 00:11:21.410
- How did you learn that?

00:11:23.890 --> 00:11:26.570
- Dude, I was so bad at English in school.

00:11:26.570 --> 00:11:28.160
So to clarify, right.

00:11:28.160 --> 00:11:30.850
Okay, I'll just start the story with this.

00:11:30.850 --> 00:11:32.480
We'll start strong, right.

00:11:32.480 --> 00:11:36.030
I was so bad at English that
they put me with the kids

00:11:36.030 --> 00:11:41.030
who you know we're not
good at anything, you know?

00:11:41.364 --> 00:11:42.430
- Yeah.

00:11:42.430 --> 00:11:43.390
- Yeah.

00:11:43.390 --> 00:11:45.550
I was in the English class for one year

00:11:45.550 --> 00:11:47.210
with kids with learning disabilities.

00:11:47.210 --> 00:11:48.043
- Right.

00:11:48.043 --> 00:11:50.636
And I remember being dude, what the fuck?

00:11:50.636 --> 00:11:51.870
(all laugh)

00:11:51.870 --> 00:11:52.703
- Because okay.

00:11:52.703 --> 00:11:55.640
I've always been really good
at most subjects in school

00:11:55.640 --> 00:11:57.953
and, okay to clarify the reason
why my English was so bad

00:11:57.953 --> 00:12:00.827
is because the only reading
and writing I ever did

00:12:00.827 --> 00:12:02.090
was in Welsh.

00:12:02.090 --> 00:12:04.320
Because my school was Welsh.

00:12:04.320 --> 00:12:07.070
Everything I spoke in school,
and read was in Welsh.

00:12:07.070 --> 00:12:09.440
But I obviously knew how to spell English.

00:12:09.440 --> 00:12:11.169
Speak English obviously.

00:12:11.169 --> 00:12:14.280
And then yeah, I remember we
did an English spelling test

00:12:14.280 --> 00:12:16.010
and I got everything wrong.

00:12:16.010 --> 00:12:17.460
But bear in mind I was like eight.

00:12:17.460 --> 00:12:19.247
And I remember they said like

00:12:19.247 --> 00:12:20.957
"Oh, can you smell the woods said for us?"

00:12:20.957 --> 00:12:22.596
And I was like, "Yeah sure."

00:12:22.596 --> 00:12:23.646
And I just-

00:12:23.646 --> 00:12:24.479
- S-E-D.

00:12:24.479 --> 00:12:25.312
- S-E-D.

00:12:25.312 --> 00:12:26.633
- I put like Z-E-D.

00:12:28.250 --> 00:12:30.088
And then my parents were like, "Oh no."

00:12:30.088 --> 00:12:30.921
(Joey and Garnt laugh)

00:12:30.921 --> 00:12:33.243
- Bear in mind, I never
read anything in English.

00:12:33.243 --> 00:12:34.076
Reading at all.

00:12:34.076 --> 00:12:35.290
It was just always video games.

00:12:35.290 --> 00:12:36.123
So, yeah.

00:12:36.123 --> 00:12:37.679
And I forgot why was I...

00:12:37.679 --> 00:12:38.512
Why did this story come up?

00:12:38.512 --> 00:12:39.451
I forgot why I was saying this now.

00:12:39.451 --> 00:12:40.990
(indistinct chatter)

00:12:40.990 --> 00:12:43.403
- Yeah, so I think I
learned how to write...

00:12:43.403 --> 00:12:46.020
Because in English as well, in school

00:12:46.020 --> 00:12:48.130
they teach you the stroke order.

00:12:48.130 --> 00:12:48.963
- Do they?

00:12:48.963 --> 00:12:50.067
I can't remember this.

00:12:50.067 --> 00:12:52.020
- I learnt it when we had to...

00:12:52.020 --> 00:12:53.620
I don't know if this is only in Australia

00:12:53.620 --> 00:12:56.250
but I think I was in
fourth grade or something

00:12:56.250 --> 00:12:57.920
- Yeah, because you have those
papers which are half width

00:12:57.920 --> 00:12:58.753
and full width.

00:12:58.753 --> 00:12:59.586
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:12:59.586 --> 00:13:00.419
And you have to.

00:13:00.419 --> 00:13:03.130
I learned how to do it when
we learned to write cursive.

00:13:03.130 --> 00:13:04.220
- Yeah, because I
remember learning cursive,

00:13:04.220 --> 00:13:06.692
and it kind of became a
thing where I for some reason

00:13:06.692 --> 00:13:08.487
I just started writing
some of them weirdly,

00:13:08.487 --> 00:13:09.913
and no one ever stopped me.

00:13:11.091 --> 00:13:12.059
- I do what I want.

00:13:12.059 --> 00:13:13.300
- And so I've always done.

00:13:13.300 --> 00:13:15.160
I'll go into the A and then I'll go down

00:13:15.160 --> 00:13:16.990
and then do the S up and then slash down.

00:13:16.990 --> 00:13:19.560
- How do you write the number five.

00:13:19.560 --> 00:13:21.810
Do you go from the bottom
or do you go from the top?

00:13:21.810 --> 00:13:22.990
- It depends, I guess.

00:13:22.990 --> 00:13:24.020
Whatever the situation.

00:13:24.020 --> 00:13:24.870
- What do you mean it depends?

00:13:24.870 --> 00:13:26.740
- Yeah, I don't know.

00:13:26.740 --> 00:13:27.860
- How does that work?

00:13:27.860 --> 00:13:30.191
- There's only one way to do it.

00:13:30.191 --> 00:13:31.210
- Most of the time I
would do it from the top,

00:13:31.210 --> 00:13:32.160
but I remember distinctively

00:13:32.160 --> 00:13:33.460
I was doing it from the bottom for a while

00:13:33.460 --> 00:13:34.470
and then I stopped that.

00:13:34.470 --> 00:13:37.450
But I also used to write my fours like...

00:13:37.450 --> 00:13:38.400
The correct way of doing...

00:13:38.400 --> 00:13:40.160
How do you learn to
wright fours in Australia.

00:13:40.160 --> 00:13:41.550
- I do it this way.

00:13:41.550 --> 00:13:42.650
I do it that way.

00:13:42.650 --> 00:13:43.640
- That's the way I learned.

00:13:43.640 --> 00:13:46.000
But then I remember I was
playing brain training

00:13:46.000 --> 00:13:47.887
and they wouldn't accept
that way of writing four.

00:13:47.887 --> 00:13:48.970
(Joey and Garnt laugh)

00:13:48.970 --> 00:13:50.100
This is when I was like 11.

00:13:50.100 --> 00:13:51.850
So then I started having to write fours

00:13:51.850 --> 00:13:55.360
in the Americanized way,
which is doing that way.

00:13:55.360 --> 00:13:56.193
- Like that?

00:13:56.193 --> 00:13:57.360
- That's the Americanized way?

00:13:57.360 --> 00:14:00.020
- Well, I think so, yeah.

00:14:00.020 --> 00:14:02.620
It looks a a kind of spiky nine, right?

00:14:02.620 --> 00:14:05.030
- I don't think I've
write any letters starting

00:14:05.030 --> 00:14:06.460
from the bottom.

00:14:06.460 --> 00:14:07.877
I'm always-

00:14:07.877 --> 00:14:09.600
- Wait, how do you do your fours?

00:14:09.600 --> 00:14:11.000
- Like this.

00:14:11.000 --> 00:14:12.770
- I do it the opposite way, I think.

00:14:12.770 --> 00:14:13.792
Yeah, yeah.

00:14:13.792 --> 00:14:14.625
- So you do it from the bottom?

00:14:14.625 --> 00:14:15.458
- Yeah, from the bottom, and then I go-

00:14:15.458 --> 00:14:16.450
- How the fuck do you do that?

00:14:16.450 --> 00:14:17.283
- I don't know.

00:14:17.283 --> 00:14:18.116
- Yeah, this feels so weird.

00:14:18.116 --> 00:14:20.090
- So in school, did you have to learn

00:14:20.090 --> 00:14:22.330
English literature and language?

00:14:22.330 --> 00:14:23.938
- What's the difference?

00:14:23.938 --> 00:14:25.851
- Because they were two different
subjects for us in school.

00:14:25.851 --> 00:14:27.090
- Oh no, we just had English.

00:14:27.090 --> 00:14:29.740
- Shit, cause see, I had
to learn English literature

00:14:29.740 --> 00:14:32.860
English language, Welsh
literature and Welsh language.

00:14:32.860 --> 00:14:34.370
I fucking hated doing that many.

00:14:34.370 --> 00:14:36.990
Okay, cause I think for us,
maybe it's just my school.

00:14:36.990 --> 00:14:39.653
But it depended on the day of the week.

00:14:40.700 --> 00:14:43.610
It was like on Mondays we
go through a literature

00:14:43.610 --> 00:14:45.300
for the term that we have to study.

00:14:45.300 --> 00:14:48.820
And then on Wednesdays we
got to do something else

00:14:48.820 --> 00:14:52.110
watch a movie or study a
different text for a certain thing

00:14:52.110 --> 00:14:55.570
or how to read an essay and
write an essay on Fridays.

00:14:55.570 --> 00:14:56.403
And shit like that.

00:14:56.403 --> 00:14:57.630
So yeah, we didn't...

00:14:57.630 --> 00:15:00.720
I think it's because my school
was just very small as well.

00:15:00.720 --> 00:15:02.820
So they probably wasn't
enough English teachers

00:15:02.820 --> 00:15:03.977
in our school to be like,

00:15:03.977 --> 00:15:04.810
"You're the literature one,

00:15:04.810 --> 00:15:06.377
and you're the comprehension one."

00:15:07.320 --> 00:15:10.160
- How does it feel learning a
new language as your older now

00:15:10.160 --> 00:15:11.440
though, compared to when you were a kid.

00:15:11.440 --> 00:15:13.610
Because I remember we had
to learn a lot of the other

00:15:13.610 --> 00:15:15.820
languages when were in school.

00:15:15.820 --> 00:15:17.920
We had to learn Spanish, French.

00:15:17.920 --> 00:15:19.210
- Didn't take any of that shit-

00:15:19.210 --> 00:15:20.760
- No.

00:15:20.760 --> 00:15:23.010
- But it's been a really
different challenge

00:15:23.010 --> 00:15:25.280
learning Japanese as a grown adult.

00:15:25.280 --> 00:15:26.467
I would say.

00:15:26.467 --> 00:15:30.630
Because I don't know, has the fact that

00:15:30.630 --> 00:15:32.660
you are very much into Japanese culture

00:15:32.660 --> 00:15:35.290
and watching anime helped you
at all from your perspective.

00:15:35.290 --> 00:15:36.278
- Yeah, definitely.

00:15:36.278 --> 00:15:37.720
I think it's made it easier,

00:15:37.720 --> 00:15:40.900
but easy with an asterisk, right?

00:15:40.900 --> 00:15:42.142
- Yeah.

00:15:42.142 --> 00:15:44.665
- Easier to understand
some concepts culturally

00:15:44.665 --> 00:15:46.020
that might explain some of the language.

00:15:46.020 --> 00:15:47.190
Which is great.

00:15:47.190 --> 00:15:49.910
But at the end of the
day it doesn't help me

00:15:49.910 --> 00:15:51.660
in a crazy amount.

00:15:51.660 --> 00:15:52.780
I think it just helps me understand

00:15:52.780 --> 00:15:56.010
why certain things are the
way they are in a language.

00:15:56.010 --> 00:16:01.010
You know, why you can't
be direct to someone.

00:16:01.020 --> 00:16:02.523
Why it's always

00:16:02.523 --> 00:16:05.790
(speaking in Japanese)

00:16:05.790 --> 00:16:06.960
- I guess because sometimes
when you're learning

00:16:06.960 --> 00:16:09.390
the language you're, "Why
can't I just be direct?

00:16:09.390 --> 00:16:11.000
It's not a thing you can't do that.

00:16:11.000 --> 00:16:12.240
That's too aggressive.

00:16:12.240 --> 00:16:13.530
I think learning Japanese from me,

00:16:13.530 --> 00:16:16.105
I didn't realize how much I kind of just

00:16:16.105 --> 00:16:19.080
zoned out Japanese when
I'm watched anime before.

00:16:19.080 --> 00:16:19.913
- Yeah, you do.

00:16:19.913 --> 00:16:20.910
You filter it out.

00:16:20.910 --> 00:16:22.140
because you're that's nonsense to me.

00:16:22.140 --> 00:16:23.300
I'm focusing on this.

00:16:23.300 --> 00:16:25.378
You're just absorbing the subtitles.

00:16:25.378 --> 00:16:27.863
Then you kind of just
mute out the Japanese.

00:16:27.863 --> 00:16:29.732
I didn't realize that
until I started learning.

00:16:29.732 --> 00:16:32.640
When I actually picked out individual,

00:16:32.640 --> 00:16:35.890
how the sentence works and how
the language actually works.

00:16:35.890 --> 00:16:37.747
That I realized,

00:16:37.747 --> 00:16:39.828
"Oh this didn't help me a lot at all.

00:16:39.828 --> 00:16:40.885
(Joey and Garnt laugh)

00:16:40.885 --> 00:16:43.040
I find it really hard in my head

00:16:43.040 --> 00:16:46.100
to recommend learning
a language to people.

00:16:46.100 --> 00:16:49.866
Because I feel if you're
not going to actually do it,

00:16:49.866 --> 00:16:51.520
it's kind of a waste of time.

00:16:51.520 --> 00:16:52.416
- I know, it takes commitment.

00:16:52.416 --> 00:16:54.288
- That's what I said to
people though, about Japanese.

00:16:54.288 --> 00:16:56.125
- And it's one of those
things where learning Japanese

00:16:56.125 --> 00:16:58.930
especially if you're not
going to do it full time,

00:16:58.930 --> 00:17:01.272
it's like at least a five-year thing

00:17:01.272 --> 00:17:02.105
that you have to commit to.

00:17:02.105 --> 00:17:04.960
And if you quit two half years in,

00:17:04.960 --> 00:17:06.290
- But that's the problem.

00:17:06.290 --> 00:17:07.123
So many people.

00:17:07.123 --> 00:17:09.180
I get fucking emails about
it all the time goddamn time,

00:17:09.180 --> 00:17:10.930
being like. "What's the
easiest way to learn Japanese?"

00:17:10.930 --> 00:17:12.940
There is no easy way to learn Japanese.

00:17:12.940 --> 00:17:14.443
You just have to sit
down and just be like,

00:17:14.443 --> 00:17:16.830
"I'm I about to commit
five to 10 years of my life

00:17:16.830 --> 00:17:17.663
to learn this shit?"

00:17:17.663 --> 00:17:18.637
"Yes."

00:17:18.637 --> 00:17:19.470
Go for it.

00:17:19.470 --> 00:17:20.380
It's like any skill chart.

00:17:20.380 --> 00:17:23.770
Where it's the first getting

00:17:23.770 --> 00:17:25.718
over the first real difficult bump

00:17:25.718 --> 00:17:26.551
is the hardest.

00:17:26.551 --> 00:17:29.670
And once you get past that,
you've gone through a challenge.

00:17:29.670 --> 00:17:30.503
You've overcome it.

00:17:30.503 --> 00:17:32.018
Normally you could keep going.

00:17:32.018 --> 00:17:33.240
That's the same with any craft, right?

00:17:33.240 --> 00:17:35.650
Voice acting as well,
photography, anything.

00:17:35.650 --> 00:17:37.210
- YouTube.

00:17:37.210 --> 00:17:40.270
- There's always gonna be that first point

00:17:40.270 --> 00:17:42.210
where you think you're
starting to understand it.

00:17:42.210 --> 00:17:43.757
Then you get to that
