00:54:42.490 --> 00:54:44.253
I've got a different experience out of it.

00:54:44.253 --> 00:54:45.223
- I 100% agree with that.

00:54:45.223 --> 00:54:47.183
- I watched it first time
when it came out on Netflix.

00:54:47.183 --> 00:54:48.680
First time ever watching it.

00:54:48.680 --> 00:54:50.330
- How'd you find it?

00:54:50.330 --> 00:54:51.163
- It was good.

00:54:51.163 --> 00:54:55.171
I mean, I think because
it was the mega hype show

00:54:55.171 --> 00:54:56.040
that it was.

00:54:56.040 --> 00:54:57.980
I think you go in expecting too much.

00:54:57.980 --> 00:54:58.983
- Yeah.

00:54:58.983 --> 00:54:59.816
- Yeah.

00:54:59.816 --> 00:55:00.649
- I mean, I was always
happy with what I got.

00:55:00.649 --> 00:55:02.122
It was just very confusing.

00:55:02.122 --> 00:55:03.260
(Joey and Garnt laughing)

00:55:03.260 --> 00:55:04.860
That's on Anno Hideaki for you.

00:55:04.860 --> 00:55:05.693
- He was great.

00:55:05.693 --> 00:55:07.510
And I liked how he built the world

00:55:07.510 --> 00:55:09.330
as a very, very terrifying one.

00:55:09.330 --> 00:55:12.645
And I feel like a lot of
animators struggle to do that.

00:55:12.645 --> 00:55:13.964
And a truly terrifying one.

00:55:13.964 --> 00:55:16.200
- Do you have that one
anime, that as Garnt said

00:55:16.200 --> 00:55:18.165
is life-changing for you?

00:55:18.165 --> 00:55:19.123
- Yeah.

00:55:19.960 --> 00:55:21.410
I mean, we spoke about it last episode,

00:55:21.410 --> 00:55:23.430
which fucked up the recording by the way.

00:55:23.430 --> 00:55:25.520
But Bokurano is definitely
one of those shows

00:55:25.520 --> 00:55:28.808
that I think definitely changed.

00:55:28.808 --> 00:55:30.380
Because again, I think
it was a similar thing

00:55:30.380 --> 00:55:32.327
where I was at a point where

00:55:32.327 --> 00:55:35.100
I think I was really confused
with what I wanted in my life.

00:55:35.100 --> 00:55:38.000
And it really helped ground me a lot,

00:55:38.000 --> 00:55:40.070
and really understand a lot of emotions

00:55:40.070 --> 00:55:41.140
that I was perhaps feeling.

00:55:41.140 --> 00:55:42.670
- Can we re-talk about Bokurano,

00:55:42.670 --> 00:55:45.398
because I want the audience
to know about Bokurano.

00:55:45.398 --> 00:55:47.040
- Not enough people have
seen Bokurano unfortunately.

00:55:47.040 --> 00:55:48.640
- It's one of those shows where,

00:55:49.590 --> 00:55:51.240
it's not the best show,

00:55:51.240 --> 00:55:52.420
but it's a very important one

00:55:52.420 --> 00:55:54.481
that I think people should watch.

00:55:54.481 --> 00:55:56.930
And I don't know how to
describe that eloquently.

00:55:56.930 --> 00:55:58.840
- It's very disturbing but not

00:55:58.840 --> 00:56:01.598
for the conventional
reason for being disturbed.

00:56:01.598 --> 00:56:05.970
- What Bokurano is about is,
there's these group of kids

00:56:05.970 --> 00:56:07.472
- This is going to sound
awesome by the way.

00:56:07.472 --> 00:56:08.954
(all laughing)

00:56:08.954 --> 00:56:11.275
- Because it sounds like
an Evangelion rip off.

00:56:11.275 --> 00:56:12.108
Yeah.

00:56:12.108 --> 00:56:12.941
- It really does.

00:56:12.941 --> 00:56:13.774
- Because there's these group of kids

00:56:13.774 --> 00:56:15.920
and then, I think they were
on a school trip or something.

00:56:15.920 --> 00:56:17.293
- They're on a school trip.

00:56:18.730 --> 00:56:20.180
- All I remember is they find his cave

00:56:20.180 --> 00:56:22.303
with a talking head or something that.

00:56:22.303 --> 00:56:23.520
- No, so there's a guy in a cave

00:56:23.520 --> 00:56:27.100
and he's a middle-aged man
working on a PC in a cave.

00:56:27.100 --> 00:56:28.473
It's really weird set up.

00:56:29.806 --> 00:56:31.207
And he basically asked them,
"Do you wanna play a game?"

00:56:31.207 --> 00:56:32.610
- Would you to play a game?

00:56:32.610 --> 00:56:35.070
- Which, you know, anyone
asking you that ever

00:56:35.070 --> 00:56:37.412
with a bunch of kids is
an immediate no, no, no.

00:56:37.412 --> 00:56:38.245
(Joey and Garnt laughing)

00:56:38.245 --> 00:56:39.960
And then I think they all
get on a scale or something.

00:56:39.960 --> 00:56:41.290
They all take turns, he measures them.

00:56:41.290 --> 00:56:42.647
Then whatever happens.

00:56:42.647 --> 00:56:44.620
And then suddenly they go outside

00:56:44.620 --> 00:56:46.332
or happens later on in that evening.

00:56:46.332 --> 00:56:47.165
Because they were all...

00:56:47.165 --> 00:56:48.370
We get to know these
characters a little bit.

00:56:48.370 --> 00:56:50.285
There's how many kids is there?

00:56:50.285 --> 00:56:51.118
12.

00:56:51.118 --> 00:56:51.951
- It's like 12, 13.

00:56:51.951 --> 00:56:52.784
Something that around that many kids.

00:56:52.784 --> 00:56:56.170
And then they get teleported
into this huge mech

00:56:56.170 --> 00:56:58.910
and there's a scary floating
head that's talking to them.

00:56:58.910 --> 00:57:01.970
And one of the children
has to pilot the Mech.

00:57:01.970 --> 00:57:04.545
And now we're going to go
into spoil this, a little bit.

00:57:04.545 --> 00:57:05.378
But yeah, it's it's episode one.

00:57:05.378 --> 00:57:07.787
So I'm going to spoil the
premise a little bit to you.

00:57:07.787 --> 00:57:09.754
So one of the kids, pilots, the mech,

00:57:09.754 --> 00:57:11.070
and they're finding another mech.

00:57:11.070 --> 00:57:12.680
And it's to save the
world that they're told

00:57:12.680 --> 00:57:13.853
before this floating head character.

00:57:13.853 --> 00:57:15.463
- A very intimidating character.

00:57:16.410 --> 00:57:17.500
They win the battle.

00:57:17.500 --> 00:57:19.940
Hooray, they all win they all
celebrate and they go outside.

00:57:19.940 --> 00:57:20.950
They stand on the mech

00:57:20.950 --> 00:57:23.190
and then one of the kids just drops dead

00:57:23.190 --> 00:57:24.660
and falls off the mech.

00:57:24.660 --> 00:57:27.557
Then they find out that each
time this mech comes back

00:57:27.557 --> 00:57:28.410
and they're summoned,

00:57:28.410 --> 00:57:30.190
one of the kids has to pilots the mech.

00:57:30.190 --> 00:57:32.587
And when they do, they're
gonna, die immediately after

00:57:32.587 --> 00:57:33.950
but it's to save the world.

00:57:33.950 --> 00:57:38.250
- Yeah, and what the
real beauty of this show

00:57:38.250 --> 00:57:41.060
isn't really the mech
battles or the make fights.

00:57:41.060 --> 00:57:43.660
It's more of the fact that these kids

00:57:43.660 --> 00:57:46.100
who have to pilot the
mech to save the world.

00:57:46.100 --> 00:57:48.674
It's basically kind of
a monster that we show.

00:57:48.674 --> 00:57:50.460
Every week a new monster comes along.

00:57:50.460 --> 00:57:52.560
And the new kid, another
kid from that group

00:57:52.560 --> 00:57:54.010
has to pilot the mech.

00:57:54.010 --> 00:57:57.367
But it's about the backstory
of each of the kids.

00:57:57.367 --> 00:57:59.773
And just having to deal with the fact

00:57:59.773 --> 00:58:02.410
that they're gonna die.

00:58:02.410 --> 00:58:03.340
They're just going to die.

00:58:03.340 --> 00:58:07.530
- And in really realistic ways as well.

00:58:07.530 --> 00:58:09.800
These characters are very believable.

00:58:09.800 --> 00:58:12.380
- It makes me uncomfortable,
even thinking back

00:58:12.380 --> 00:58:14.710
to the emotions it brought out to me.

00:58:14.710 --> 00:58:16.020
I get very...

00:58:17.570 --> 00:58:19.870
It's a really, really brutally honest look

00:58:19.870 --> 00:58:22.550
into the human condition and life.

00:58:22.550 --> 00:58:25.940
And especially how, you
know, a lot of these kids

00:58:25.940 --> 00:58:27.030
from a lot of different backgrounds.

00:58:27.030 --> 00:58:28.200
Some of them have it easier.

00:58:28.200 --> 00:58:29.810
I remember there's a one
kid who's the stereotypical

00:58:29.810 --> 00:58:30.787
piece of shit.

00:58:30.787 --> 00:58:31.700
His that spoiled..

00:58:31.700 --> 00:58:32.960
- Of course.

00:58:32.960 --> 00:58:34.630
- But there's some of the kids who,

00:58:34.630 --> 00:58:36.660
I think there's one kid
who's 16 or whatever.

00:58:36.660 --> 00:58:39.610
And he's looking after his two siblings.

00:58:39.610 --> 00:58:41.630
It's brutal, because he's
the one who's raising

00:58:41.630 --> 00:58:43.520
his two sisters, I think.

00:58:43.520 --> 00:58:45.820
It's horrible, seeing
him after come to terms

00:58:45.820 --> 00:58:48.050
with that he's not gonna be
able to look after his sister.

00:58:48.050 --> 00:58:49.980
It's really brutal.

00:58:49.980 --> 00:58:53.160
It's something that just
disturbs you on a level

00:58:53.160 --> 00:58:54.130
that you can't really describe.

00:58:54.130 --> 00:58:56.218
It's so raw, it's so realistic.

00:58:56.218 --> 00:58:58.495
No filters whatsoever.

00:58:58.495 --> 00:59:01.680
- It's something that
really was not many people

00:59:01.680 --> 00:59:03.020
have watched.

00:59:03.020 --> 00:59:04.607
It's something that was
really glossed over.

00:59:04.607 --> 00:59:05.440
It's uncomfortable.

00:59:05.440 --> 00:59:06.990
It's really uncomfortable
to have to sit down

00:59:06.990 --> 00:59:07.823
and sit through.

00:59:07.823 --> 00:59:09.663
- I admit, I definitely did not watch it

00:59:09.663 --> 00:59:11.160
when it first came out.

00:59:11.160 --> 00:59:12.510
I definitely gave it some time.

00:59:12.510 --> 00:59:15.510
- It'd definitely not a, "Yo,
you watched the last episode?"

00:59:17.598 --> 00:59:19.367
- Cause I think the problem with Bokurano,

00:59:19.367 --> 00:59:20.210
and the reason why

00:59:20.210 --> 00:59:21.810
so many people didn't
watch it when it came out,

00:59:21.810 --> 00:59:24.370
is because the way that they marketed it,

00:59:24.370 --> 00:59:26.480
was not that good, not that accurate.

00:59:26.480 --> 00:59:27.436
A lot of people are like,

00:59:27.436 --> 00:59:28.269
"It's a mecha.

00:59:28.269 --> 00:59:29.640
Must just being Evangelion rip off."

00:59:29.640 --> 00:59:32.250
- There's no world where
it's the number one anime.

00:59:32.250 --> 00:59:33.540
cause it's just too uncomfortable.

00:59:33.540 --> 00:59:34.870
- Yeah.

00:59:34.870 --> 00:59:36.220
- It also came out in the time period.

00:59:36.220 --> 00:59:38.790
Cause I think it was
the early to mid 2000s.

00:59:38.790 --> 00:59:39.803
- It was.

00:59:39.803 --> 00:59:42.744
- where there was just so
many Evangelion rip offs.

00:59:42.744 --> 00:59:45.610
They they're of varying quality as well.

00:59:45.610 --> 00:59:47.250
There's another show that
I fucking love as well,

00:59:47.250 --> 00:59:48.200
which is Rahxephon.

00:59:49.650 --> 00:59:51.551
- That's just an Evangelion rip off.

00:59:51.551 --> 00:59:52.890
- I have no idea what that is.

00:59:52.890 --> 00:59:55.520
- It's an Evangelion rip off
but it's still really good.

00:59:55.520 --> 00:59:57.320
- It's really good.

00:59:57.320 --> 00:59:59.410
It's totally rips off,
but it goes about it

00:59:59.410 --> 01:00:01.450
in a totally different
way from Evangelion.

01:00:01.450 --> 01:00:04.740
Bokurano also sits in this
category of just shows

01:00:04.740 --> 01:00:06.230
that people have really looked over.

01:00:06.230 --> 01:00:08.370
Cause the premise alone
sounds an Evangelion rip off.

01:00:08.370 --> 01:00:09.520
- It does, it does.

01:00:09.520 --> 01:00:13.520
But the way they go about it
is just absolutely harrowing.

01:00:13.520 --> 01:00:16.010
Just seeing these stories of these kids

01:00:16.010 --> 01:00:18.500
who have to come to terms
with their own mortality.

01:00:18.500 --> 01:00:20.190
Cause it's a fucking tragedy.

01:00:20.190 --> 01:00:21.023
- Yeah, it is.

01:00:21.023 --> 01:00:22.340
- It's different from Evangelion.

01:00:22.340 --> 01:00:27.030
Evangelion to me is just
Anno's raw cry for help.

01:00:27.030 --> 01:00:28.000
You know what I mean?

01:00:28.000 --> 01:00:28.833
- Yeah.

01:00:29.833 --> 01:00:33.760
- Everyone's analyzed last
two episodes of Evangelion.

01:00:35.129 --> 01:00:36.690
I think it's going back to that meme

01:00:36.690 --> 01:00:38.670
about the blue curtain.

01:00:38.670 --> 01:00:41.210
I'm fucking sure that
Ano had no fucking clue

01:00:41.210 --> 01:00:42.043
what he was doing.

01:00:42.043 --> 01:00:44.370
- Everyone is like, "Oh, okay,
the way that these lines move

01:00:44.370 --> 01:00:45.830
and the way that it's very sketchy,

01:00:45.830 --> 01:00:48.570
is like really reflective
on Shinji's mental state."

01:00:48.570 --> 01:00:49.797
Meanwhile, Ano is just like,

01:00:49.797 --> 01:00:51.590
"We didn't have much of a budget.

01:00:51.590 --> 01:00:53.130
just wanna put that out there."

01:00:53.130 --> 01:00:56.110
That's why I love about Evangelion.

01:00:56.110 --> 01:00:58.950
Because everyone comes out of Evangelion

01:00:58.950 --> 01:01:00.240
with something different.

01:01:00.240 --> 01:01:02.900
Because his message was so raw

01:01:02.900 --> 01:01:05.480
and he puts so much of
himself into the series.

01:01:05.480 --> 01:01:07.572
That it's impossible
not to come out with it

01:01:07.572 --> 01:01:08.405
feeling something.

01:01:08.405 --> 01:01:11.230
- I love how with Evangelion
especially that I don't know

01:01:11.230 --> 01:01:13.820
if it's just Anno is
just trolling like crazy.

01:01:13.820 --> 01:01:17.437
But there were moments where
the Evangelion fan base

01:01:17.437 --> 01:01:20.740
and the super hardcore
analysts, Evangelion

01:01:20.740 --> 01:01:23.820
are just so committed to this idea of

01:01:23.820 --> 01:01:27.075
everything in Evangelion,
every piece of imagery.

01:01:27.075 --> 01:01:28.870
Everything has to have a meaning,

01:01:28.870 --> 01:01:33.090
that I remember when Anno
finally came out in an interview

01:01:33.090 --> 01:01:34.820
about the meaning behind Evangelion

01:01:34.820 --> 01:01:37.750
and he just straight up
said, there is no meaning.

01:01:37.750 --> 01:01:38.990
It's just the show I wanted to make.

01:01:38.990 --> 01:01:40.850
And people were like, "But
what about the fact that

01:01:40.850 --> 01:01:43.080
every time the angels die
it turns into a cross.

01:01:43.080 --> 01:01:45.010
And he's like, "I just
thought that looked cool."

01:01:45.010 --> 01:01:48.310
And all the analysts are
like, "No, no he's lying.

01:01:48.310 --> 01:01:50.440
There has to be a meaning behind it."

01:01:50.440 --> 01:01:52.400
if the creator says there's no meaning,

01:01:52.400 --> 01:01:53.430
there's no meaning, bro.

01:01:53.430 --> 01:01:56.220
- What's Occam's razor
where the simplest solution-

01:01:56.220 --> 01:01:57.880
- The simplest solution
is the best solution.

01:01:57.880 --> 01:01:59.477
- Is normally the actual solution.

01:01:59.477 --> 01:02:00.553
- Yeah.

01:02:00.553 --> 01:02:02.330
- And even though he indefinitely

01:02:02.330 --> 01:02:05.190
made me uncomfortable and feel bad

01:02:05.190 --> 01:02:06.880
for a lot of the characters.

01:02:06.880 --> 01:02:09.580
Bokurano just went way deeper.

01:02:09.580 --> 01:02:12.710
- I'd say Evangelion isn't from a story.

01:02:12.710 --> 01:02:14.404
- They're not even remotely similar.

01:02:14.404 --> 01:02:17.154
- It's not even remotely similar.

01:02:18.177 --> 01:02:20.490
Bokurano, I feel like
has more of a structure

01:02:20.490 --> 01:02:21.400
around its plots.

01:02:21.400 --> 01:02:24.380
Where Evangelion just ended on this,

01:02:24.380 --> 01:02:27.692
as I said, raw cry for help from Anno.

01:02:27.692 --> 01:02:29.473
But Bokurano was definitely

01:02:29.473 --> 01:02:32.250
here's a group of kids
dealing with something

01:02:32.250 --> 01:02:33.980
that's very very uncomfortable

01:02:33.980 --> 01:02:36.817
and you're going to feel
fucking awful watching the show.

01:02:36.817 --> 01:02:39.870
It's not even the worst part
that kids are gonna die.

01:02:39.870 --> 01:02:43.910
It's like, sometimes it's
their backstories are horrific.

01:02:43.910 --> 01:02:46.485
And I'm not gonna say it,
because I don't wanna spoil it

01:02:46.485 --> 01:02:47.318
because it's a really good one.

01:02:47.318 --> 01:02:49.590
But there was one episode in particular.

01:02:49.590 --> 01:02:50.720
And after I finished it,

01:02:50.720 --> 01:02:51.730
it was one of the things
where I had to like

01:02:51.730 --> 01:02:53.150
just sit there for five minutes

01:02:53.150 --> 01:02:54.807
and be like, "Fuck, fuck."

01:02:57.949 --> 01:03:00.050
I don't know if you can
remember all the episodes.

01:03:00.050 --> 01:03:01.697
There's one or two plots.

01:03:01.697 --> 01:03:03.357
One of the stories, where I was just like,

01:03:03.357 --> 01:03:04.630
"Fuck, Jesus Christ."

01:03:04.630 --> 01:03:05.700
It was right at the end.

01:03:05.700 --> 01:03:06.811
It was the episode.

01:03:06.811 --> 01:03:08.510
Then you think that you
expected everything, right?

01:03:08.510 --> 01:03:09.343
Yeah.

01:03:09.343 --> 01:03:11.940
That's what I love though
about these human drama shows.

01:03:11.940 --> 01:03:14.640
Is that sometimes they may
just be the simplest thing

01:03:14.640 --> 01:03:18.210
of just a story between
two people or one person.

01:03:18.210 --> 01:03:21.130
But if it's done really well, it can be

01:03:21.130 --> 01:03:23.490
some of the most powerful storytelling.

01:03:23.490 --> 01:03:26.410
- I think it's more
relatable than most things.

01:03:26.410 --> 01:03:28.140
And it's really uncomfortable to think

01:03:28.140 --> 01:03:30.060
that you could be in a situation where

01:03:30.060 --> 01:03:31.690
you have to come to terms with your death.

01:03:31.690 --> 01:03:35.610
That's why I'll say this
till the end of time,

01:03:35.610 --> 01:03:37.207
but like that's the whole
reason why my favorite

01:03:37.207 --> 01:03:39.408
[indistinct] of all time is Inio Asano.

01:03:39.408 --> 01:03:42.190
- I was gonna say, the one series

01:03:42.190 --> 01:03:44.380
the one manga series
that I'm still waiting on

01:03:44.380 --> 01:03:47.677
to be in the right head space
to read is Oyasumi Punpun.

01:03:47.677 --> 01:03:50.260
(indistinct chatter)

01:03:50.260 --> 01:03:52.957
Because I've read that, I've
re-read that two or three times

01:03:52.957 --> 01:03:56.957
all the way through, and
every time, I'm just like,

01:03:56.957 --> 01:03:58.533
"Oh no."

01:03:58.533 --> 01:04:00.210
That's the only way it's just, "Oh, no."

01:04:00.210 --> 01:04:03.010
Because it's just so...

01:04:03.010 --> 01:04:04.550
It's not just Punpun as well.

01:04:04.550 --> 01:04:08.780
Inio Asano is just so good
at writing these characters

01:04:08.780 --> 01:04:11.190
that are just so believable.

01:04:11.190 --> 01:04:14.090
And it's really disturbing
when you see these characters,

01:04:14.090 --> 01:04:15.700
these very believable characters.

01:04:15.700 --> 01:04:19.530
Run into these very believable
and horrifying situations.

01:04:19.530 --> 01:04:21.280
And you're just ah.

01:04:21.280 --> 01:04:23.960
If this isn't based off
a real person's life,

01:04:23.960 --> 01:04:25.690
then that's just scary in it of itself.

01:04:25.690 --> 01:04:28.840
Because this guy can
just think of stuff this.

