(indistinct chatter)

01:51:17.313 --> 01:51:18.680
- I'll go on for you friend.

01:51:18.680 --> 01:51:20.468
- I'll see you in the finals.

01:51:20.468 --> 01:51:21.760
(all laugh)

01:51:21.760 --> 01:51:22.593
- And then it's weird.

01:51:22.593 --> 01:51:23.426
Cause I never had any...

01:51:23.426 --> 01:51:24.530
A lot of these kids as well.

01:51:24.530 --> 01:51:26.027
They would be studying
it in between games,

01:51:26.027 --> 01:51:29.146
but I would just whip out
Pokemon at start playing it.

01:51:29.146 --> 01:51:31.260
Then I'll be like, "It's my
time to go and save and play."

01:51:31.260 --> 01:51:32.910
But I remember, so my fifth game,

01:51:32.910 --> 01:51:34.660
was against the guy, I beat in my school.

01:51:34.660 --> 01:51:36.227
The prodigy team or whatever.

01:51:36.227 --> 01:51:38.490
And I had to play him again and we drew.

01:51:38.490 --> 01:51:39.720
It was really anti-climactic.

01:51:39.720 --> 01:51:41.210
I was like, "Fuck, I beat him last time,

01:51:41.210 --> 01:51:42.620
I wanna beat him again."

01:51:42.620 --> 01:51:45.130
Anyway, I got on the team and I was okay.

01:51:45.130 --> 01:51:46.030
I was struggling.

01:51:46.030 --> 01:51:48.530
Cause this is where it was
getting really serious.

01:51:50.183 --> 01:51:53.080
I was decent enough where I
could win 70% of my games,

01:51:53.080 --> 01:51:55.746
but it was still starting
to get really long.

01:51:55.746 --> 01:51:58.130
Because chess games never
went more than an hour.

01:51:58.130 --> 01:52:00.200
And then they start becoming two hours.

01:52:00.200 --> 01:52:02.060
And I'm 13.

01:52:02.060 --> 01:52:03.700
And like, "This is [indistinct]."

01:52:03.700 --> 01:52:04.877
- I just want to play-

01:52:04.877 --> 01:52:06.292
(indistinct chatter)

01:52:06.292 --> 01:52:08.027
I start winning and then I got
content and they were like,

01:52:08.027 --> 01:52:09.410
"Hey, do you wanna play for your country?"

01:52:09.410 --> 01:52:12.130
And I was like, "Sure, I guess
I'll play for my country."

01:52:12.130 --> 01:52:12.963
Why not?

01:52:12.963 --> 01:52:13.796
Yeah, I'm doing good enough.

01:52:13.796 --> 01:52:16.450
So I turn up, I go to
the first tournament.

01:52:16.450 --> 01:52:18.500
You won't believe because I was number 10.

01:52:18.500 --> 01:52:20.270
So there's 10 seats.

01:52:20.270 --> 01:52:21.560
1 is the best 10 is the worst.

01:52:21.560 --> 01:52:24.243
So I was the worst on the country.

01:52:24.243 --> 01:52:25.980
Worst for the country for team.

01:52:25.980 --> 01:52:27.300
Guess who was number one.

01:52:27.300 --> 01:52:29.310
I think I've told you guys this story.

01:52:29.310 --> 01:52:31.485
It was the main bully at my school.

01:52:31.485 --> 01:52:32.551
(Joey and Garnt laugh)

01:52:32.551 --> 01:52:33.407
I shit you not.

01:52:33.407 --> 01:52:34.240
- You can't make this shit up.

01:52:34.240 --> 01:52:35.402
You can't make this shit up.

01:52:35.402 --> 01:52:37.890
- I shit you not, it was
the main bully at my school

01:52:37.890 --> 01:52:40.490
who no one knew he did this.

01:52:40.490 --> 01:52:43.148
- This is the point in the manga
where the flashback begins.

01:52:43.148 --> 01:52:44.227
- Yeah.

01:52:44.227 --> 01:52:45.930
- He used to bully me.

01:52:45.930 --> 01:52:47.610
- He was the main rival all along.

01:52:47.610 --> 01:52:50.497
- He literally was the kid
that everyone was scared of.

01:52:50.497 --> 01:52:51.980
And I remember thinking man,

01:52:51.980 --> 01:52:53.730
he was really good at Halo Wars too.

01:52:53.730 --> 01:52:55.143
That was weird.

01:52:56.070 --> 01:52:59.110
Then suddenly he's really good at chess.

01:52:59.110 --> 01:53:02.046
He was amazing, and he
was winning a lot against

01:53:02.046 --> 01:53:04.360
really really good players.

01:53:04.360 --> 01:53:05.760
Bear in mind, when it got to this point

01:53:05.760 --> 01:53:08.961
it was pretty much me, him and eight kids

01:53:08.961 --> 01:53:11.016
who were gonna go to Cambridge.

01:53:11.016 --> 01:53:11.874
You know what I mean?

01:53:11.874 --> 01:53:14.410
The environment was really weird as well.

01:53:14.410 --> 01:53:16.150
And I remember just, that
was when I really started

01:53:16.150 --> 01:53:17.670
to not enjoy chess anymore.

01:53:17.670 --> 01:53:20.520
Is that when I remember,
when I lost the game,

01:53:20.520 --> 01:53:23.080
I got fucked bollocked by the coaches.

01:53:23.080 --> 01:53:25.730
They were furious at me, because
they would take your sheet.

01:53:25.730 --> 01:53:27.050
Because this is when you had
to start writing it down,

01:53:27.050 --> 01:53:27.990
they would take your sheet,

01:53:27.990 --> 01:53:29.990
and they would rinse you for your moves.

01:53:30.960 --> 01:53:33.240
And then they would
watch you the whole game.

01:53:33.240 --> 01:53:35.867
So that's always an area above
where they can watch you.

01:53:35.867 --> 01:53:37.440
(indistinct chatter)

01:53:37.440 --> 01:53:40.010
I remember if you made a move,
that was under five minutes.

01:53:40.010 --> 01:53:41.390
That was a mistake.

01:53:41.390 --> 01:53:42.914
You've got rinsed for it.

01:53:42.914 --> 01:53:44.510
Because they were like, "You
didn't think long enough."

01:53:44.510 --> 01:53:45.343
- Wow.

01:53:45.343 --> 01:53:46.320
- You've gotta go through the options.

01:53:46.320 --> 01:53:48.010
Because it gets to the
point where you're like,

01:53:48.010 --> 01:53:50.060
you know that they're
thinking just as many moves

01:53:50.060 --> 01:53:53.064
ahead as you are and it's
starting to get really difficult.

01:53:53.064 --> 01:53:55.320
Because you're like, "Fuck,
I haven't studied enough

01:53:55.320 --> 01:53:56.153
at this point."

01:53:56.153 --> 01:53:57.910
Because I never studied chess.

01:53:57.910 --> 01:53:59.500
But this is where I was
getting to the point where,

01:53:59.500 --> 01:54:01.940
I was against people who
are naturally pretty good

01:54:01.940 --> 01:54:04.948
but also were studying
all the fucking time.

01:54:04.948 --> 01:54:06.910
And it's just a really bad environment.

01:54:06.910 --> 01:54:08.110
I really didn't like it.

01:54:09.690 --> 01:54:12.320
I would finish my games
and I'd play Pokemon.

01:54:12.320 --> 01:54:14.800
They would wanna talk about,
so why did you move rook

01:54:14.800 --> 01:54:17.130
to F2, why did you do that?

01:54:17.130 --> 01:54:18.680
Because he was really
impressive when he moved his...

01:54:18.680 --> 01:54:19.930
And I was like, "I don't."

01:54:19.930 --> 01:54:20.890
(Joey and Garnt laugh)

01:54:20.890 --> 01:54:22.780
We are playing chess
for eight hours today.

01:54:22.780 --> 01:54:26.140
I do not wanna talk about
chess in between my games.

01:54:26.140 --> 01:54:28.140
It was just a really...

01:54:28.140 --> 01:54:30.960
Yeah, it was a really weird environment.

01:54:30.960 --> 01:54:33.080
I think, if I came into
chess later in my life

01:54:33.080 --> 01:54:35.920
I would've had a more
healthy enjoyment of chess.

01:54:35.920 --> 01:54:37.430
I still like to play it occasionally,

01:54:37.430 --> 01:54:40.830
but I think I'm just scarred
from the anime experience

01:54:40.830 --> 01:54:41.663
that I had.

01:54:41.663 --> 01:54:42.496
(Joey laughs)

01:54:42.496 --> 01:54:45.090
- Cause that's what I find
so fascinating about chess,

01:54:45.090 --> 01:54:47.520
is just talking to you and hearing

01:54:47.520 --> 01:54:51.129
about your chess story and
reading up and watching

01:54:51.129 --> 01:54:53.560
Magnus Carlsen I think that's his name.

01:54:53.560 --> 01:54:54.510
- Yeah, Magnus Carlsen, his one the best.

01:54:54.510 --> 01:54:56.584
- His story and how you were just like...

01:54:56.584 --> 01:54:58.706
You were just born and
you just got the game.

01:54:58.706 --> 01:55:00.710
There are people who
just studied the game.

01:55:00.710 --> 01:55:03.110
And then there are just
people who just are geniuses

01:55:03.110 --> 01:55:04.963
and they don't know why.

01:55:06.368 --> 01:55:07.301
It's fucking fascinating.

01:55:07.301 --> 01:55:09.467
It's fucking fascinating to me.

01:55:09.467 --> 01:55:12.040
- It was weird because you kind of...

01:55:12.040 --> 01:55:13.580
No matter how good you are at something,

01:55:13.580 --> 01:55:15.870
and how much raw talent
you have at something.

01:55:15.870 --> 01:55:17.720
When you start competing
at such a high level,

01:55:17.720 --> 01:55:20.430
you start to realize that
it doesn't matter as much,

01:55:20.430 --> 01:55:21.940
but also you meet people who also...

01:55:21.940 --> 01:55:24.990
There might be 10 people in that country.

01:55:24.990 --> 01:55:27.090
Who also have that same raw talent.

01:55:27.090 --> 01:55:29.020
And then it's like fuck.

01:55:29.020 --> 01:55:31.000
Cause then it starts to
come to who can put them.

01:55:31.000 --> 01:55:32.810
Cause I didn't care about chess.

01:55:32.810 --> 01:55:33.950
I never cared about chess.

01:55:33.950 --> 01:55:35.850
I was just good at it,
and I just played it.

01:55:35.850 --> 01:55:37.211
- Such a thing that a
protagonist would say.

01:55:37.211 --> 01:55:38.650
(all laugh)

01:55:38.650 --> 01:55:40.360
I never cared about chess.

01:55:40.360 --> 01:55:42.620
- Whereas the protagonist
would have got to my point lost

01:55:42.620 --> 01:55:44.736
and then been like, "I'm gonna
to dedicate my life to...

01:55:44.736 --> 01:55:45.569
(Joey and Garnt laugh)

01:55:45.569 --> 01:55:47.090
I was like, "Pokemon Ranger just came out,

01:55:47.090 --> 01:55:49.914
so I'm gonna start spinning around that.

01:55:49.914 --> 01:55:51.578
- Yeah, you took the [indistinct] route.

01:55:51.578 --> 01:55:53.656
Where you're just like, "I
lost, end of the manga."

01:55:53.656 --> 01:55:54.990
- And it was just kinda like...

01:55:54.990 --> 01:55:57.340
It gets to that point in
your life, where you're like,

01:55:57.340 --> 01:55:59.160
I don't need this anymore.

01:55:59.160 --> 01:56:00.860
I remember my parents are so sad.

01:56:00.860 --> 01:56:02.953
I don't know why my parents
were so invested in it.

01:56:02.953 --> 01:56:04.760
I think it was a mixture of proud

01:56:04.760 --> 01:56:06.540
and also they love bragging about it.

01:56:06.540 --> 01:56:07.520
Why wouldn't you do that?

01:56:07.520 --> 01:56:08.353
- Yeah, of course.

01:56:08.353 --> 01:56:11.196
- Your series got
canceled from poor sales.

01:56:11.196 --> 01:56:12.500
(all laugh)

01:56:12.500 --> 01:56:13.750
- I had a spin off.

01:56:13.750 --> 01:56:16.830
So what happened is about
when I was 16 or 17,

01:56:16.830 --> 01:56:20.350
I had a rejuvenation of my enjoyment.

01:56:20.350 --> 01:56:23.910
Do you remember a website
called MLG Game Battles?

01:56:23.910 --> 01:56:24.860
- I remember that.

01:56:24.860 --> 01:56:26.330
- It was where you could
compete against cob,

01:56:26.330 --> 01:56:27.852
but also Yahoo Chess.

01:56:27.852 --> 01:56:30.440
I remember, I would compete
against fully grown men

01:56:30.440 --> 01:56:31.560
and beat them on Yahoo Chess.

01:56:31.560 --> 01:56:32.825
They'd get so pissed off.

01:56:32.825 --> 01:56:34.104
(Joey and Garnt laugh)

01:56:34.104 --> 01:56:35.770
and then joined the local pub,

01:56:35.770 --> 01:56:37.230
and that was a weird experience.

01:56:37.230 --> 01:56:39.910
So I joined the local pub
chest team and I remember...

01:56:39.910 --> 01:56:44.330
bear in mind they were all 80
to 40 year old men, always.

01:56:44.330 --> 01:56:47.090
I remember one time I
was playing against a guy

01:56:47.090 --> 01:56:48.383
who looked Ross Kemp.

01:56:50.086 --> 01:56:51.910
A skinhead, terrifying dude.

01:56:51.910 --> 01:56:54.270
He's like this over the table.

01:56:54.270 --> 01:56:55.719
- Like a brick shit out.

01:56:55.719 --> 01:56:58.970
Every, every bouncer
you see at a nightclub.

01:56:58.970 --> 01:57:02.460
- And I'm 15, 16, like this with my Coke.

01:57:02.460 --> 01:57:04.650
And he had a pint and was smoking,

01:57:04.650 --> 01:57:07.950
I'm there with my Coke,
occasionally checking my phone.

01:57:07.950 --> 01:57:09.430
I don't know if that pissed him off

01:57:09.430 --> 01:57:11.510
but in between moves, I wouldn't
look at what he was doing.

01:57:11.510 --> 01:57:12.835
I would just check my phone.

01:57:12.835 --> 01:57:13.668
And I would like...

01:57:13.668 --> 01:57:15.070
Cause I'm normally thinking in my move.

01:57:15.070 --> 01:57:17.990
So I don't really pay much
attention about doing it.

01:57:17.990 --> 01:57:19.580
And I remember when I beat him

01:57:19.580 --> 01:57:24.580
and he looked really fucking
angry and I was so scared.

01:57:24.710 --> 01:57:28.355
I was, "Is he gonna hit me?"

01:57:28.355 --> 01:57:29.530
(Joey and Garnt laugh)

01:57:29.530 --> 01:57:30.760
He was like this on the table.

01:57:30.760 --> 01:57:31.593
Like this.

01:57:33.190 --> 01:57:34.771
I can't believe you won.

01:57:34.771 --> 01:57:35.753
- I can't believe you've done this man.

01:57:35.753 --> 01:57:37.918
- I can't believe you've done this.

01:57:37.918 --> 01:57:41.650
People didn't losing to a 15
year old, that happened a lot.

01:57:41.650 --> 01:57:43.343
- I can understand, I get it.

01:57:44.283 --> 01:57:45.680
- But you know.

01:57:45.680 --> 01:57:48.808
- I'm just really committed
to making this a manga mnow.

01:57:48.808 --> 01:57:49.641
- Honestly.

01:57:49.641 --> 01:57:51.150
- Yeah, please, cause from
a narrative perspective,

01:57:51.150 --> 01:57:52.780
there's so many interesting ways

01:57:52.780 --> 01:57:55.110
you could tackle chess just as a content.

01:57:55.110 --> 01:57:58.960
- I wanna take that concept
of your friend being beaten

01:57:58.960 --> 01:58:02.190
in the preliminary and
then just cut to the scene

01:58:02.190 --> 01:58:03.500
where you're in the final.

01:58:03.500 --> 01:58:05.610
And your friend is that
one guy who narrates

01:58:05.610 --> 01:58:06.600
all you'll moves.

01:58:06.600 --> 01:58:07.538
(all laugh)

01:58:07.538 --> 01:58:08.684
- It's a speed wagon.

01:58:08.684 --> 01:58:09.772
(indistinct chatter)

01:58:09.772 --> 01:58:11.302
- He's like, he just did a [indistinct].

01:58:11.302 --> 01:58:12.643
He's like, what's an [indistinct]

01:58:12.643 --> 01:58:15.791
is and then he just goes
along with the explanation.

01:58:15.791 --> 01:58:18.190
- Okay, this is gonna sound so nerdy.

01:58:18.190 --> 01:58:20.480
There's one move in chess
that I always wanted to use.

01:58:20.480 --> 01:58:22.500
And I don't know the name of it,

01:58:22.500 --> 01:58:24.910
but it was the one where if someone moves

01:58:24.910 --> 01:58:28.210
their pawn to and then in front of...

01:58:28.210 --> 01:58:31.820
If you move your Pawn 2,
and then move it 2 as well

01:58:31.820 --> 01:58:32.880
that you can then take it.

01:58:32.880 --> 01:58:34.172
- That's an [indistinct].

01:58:34.172 --> 01:58:35.770
- I always wanted to do that.

01:58:35.770 --> 01:58:40.550
- Dude using a castling
is Op, you always castle.

01:58:40.550 --> 01:58:41.383
That's all I remember.

01:58:41.383 --> 01:58:43.650
It says, "Why did the castle there?"

01:58:43.650 --> 01:58:45.350
It's like, I'll tell you why he's-

01:58:46.420 --> 01:58:47.510
- Yeah, I don't know.

01:58:47.510 --> 01:58:48.690
I remember they tried to teach us.

01:58:48.690 --> 01:58:49.610
They were like, "Why don't you use

01:58:49.610 --> 01:58:52.177
the Indian Prince opening of 1970?"

01:58:53.803 --> 01:58:56.140
Because when I would do an opening move,

01:58:56.140 --> 01:58:57.980
I always did the same opening
move because I just liked it.

01:58:57.980 --> 01:59:00.427
It was nice and symmetrical, I liked it.

01:59:00.427 --> 01:59:03.390
And they would always say
why did you use, this person?

01:59:03.390 --> 01:59:06.340
Yeah, like I said, the
Indian Prince move of 1764.

01:59:06.340 --> 01:59:08.940
And I was like, "What the fuck is that?"

01:59:08.940 --> 01:59:11.474
I just like how the Bishop goes to boop.

01:59:11.474 --> 01:59:13.434
(Joey and Garnt laugh)

01:59:13.434 --> 01:59:14.916
- Bishop goes, boop.

01:59:14.916 --> 01:59:16.250
It just feels nice, you know?

01:59:16.250 --> 01:59:17.083
It just feels nice.

01:59:17.083 --> 01:59:17.916
- It's hard to explain
it when you're a kid,

01:59:17.916 --> 01:59:19.610
because you're just
thinking four moves head.

01:59:19.610 --> 01:59:20.817
And you're like, if this goes
here, and this goes here,

01:59:20.817 --> 01:59:22.190
and this goes here, then you go there.

01:59:22.190 --> 01:59:23.023
You know what I mean?

01:59:23.023 --> 01:59:25.777
It's just how you see it, it was weird.

01:59:25.777 --> 01:59:27.990
It's like any sport I imagine

01:59:27.990 --> 01:59:29.527
where kids are really good at it.

01:59:29.527 --> 01:59:31.150
And the adults are really pushy

01:59:31.150 --> 01:59:33.610
and kind of almost borderline...

01:59:33.610 --> 01:59:34.980
Some of the kids I'd say they had

01:59:34.980 --> 01:59:37.400
a predatory relationship with it.

01:59:37.400 --> 01:59:39.320
Because a lot of them, again, I said

01:59:39.320 --> 01:59:41.940
they were very rich
parents whose kids went

01:59:41.940 --> 01:59:43.700
to very good private schools

01:59:43.700 --> 01:59:45.560
and they were destined to
go to Cambridge or Oxford,

01:59:45.560 --> 01:59:46.500
no matter what.

01:59:46.500 --> 01:59:48.400
And they would, you know
exactly what I mean,

01:59:48.400 --> 01:59:49.233
what kind of kids I'm talking about.

01:59:49.233 --> 01:59:50.430
Because the moment you spoke to them?

01:59:50.430 --> 01:59:53.080
You're like, we're from a different world.

01:59:53.080 --> 01:59:53.913
It's really odd.

01:59:53.913 --> 01:59:56.420
- Chess is like their
entire world to them.

01:59:56.420 --> 01:59:58.480
It was something that
was forced upon them.

01:59:58.480 --> 01:59:59.490
Cause it was, you know,

01:59:59.490 --> 02:00:00.900
it's something that
looks good on the resume

02:00:00.900 --> 02:00:02.350
when you apply for Cambridge.

02:00:03.480 --> 02:00:05.610
I mean, to be fair it
got me a few good jobs

02:00:05.610 --> 02:00:06.504
where it helped a lot.

02:00:06.504 --> 02:00:07.580
I remember some job interviews

02:00:07.580 --> 02:00:09.500
where they liked playing chess,
and they would bring it up

02:00:09.500 --> 02:00:11.900
and it was like, "Oh,
that's cute, you're good."

02:00:12.778 --> 02:00:13.611
It was like, I don't know.

02:00:13.611 --> 02:00:14.444
- That's cute.

02:00:14.444 --> 02:00:19.444
- I think that's a really
interesting story that you have.

02:00:19.754 --> 02:00:22.000
- Yeah, bottom line is we need
to turn this into an anime.

02:00:22.000 --> 02:00:22.833
- Yeah.

02:00:22.833 --> 02:00:23.740
- Most definitely.

02:00:23.740 --> 02:00:26.360
- If someone was I want
to make a chess anime.

02:00:26.360 --> 02:00:27.270
I would absolutely-

02:00:27.270 --> 02:00:28.103
- Yeah.

